 "response": {
  "text": "Yes. For **under ₹3,000**, I’d prioritize cushioning, fit, and outsole grip over flashy branding. Current listings give you several genuinely good options. [urbanstylefootwear.com](https://urbanstylefootwear.com/best-running-shoes-under-3000-india/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### My picks\n\n### [Decathlon Jogflow 100.1 M]()\n*₹1,599*\n\n### [Decathlon Jogflow 190.1 Men Cushioned]()\n*₹2,499*\n\n### [Kalenji Run Support]()\n*₹2,599*\n\n### [Kalenji Run Cushion]()\n*₹1,399*\n\n### [Kalenji Jogging Shoes]()\n*₹2,199*\n\n**1. Decathlon Jogflow 100.1 M — ₹1,599 — best overall value**  \nMy first choice for beginner-to-regular runners doing roughly 3–5 km runs. It has a strong 4.7/5 rating from 83 reviews in the current listing.\n\n**2. Decathlon Jogflow 190.1 — ₹2,499 — best if you want more cushioning**  \nWorth spending extra if you're running frequently or prefer a softer, more cushioned ride.\n\n**3. Kalenji Run Support — ₹2,599 — best for support**  \nA good option if you prefer a more supportive/stable feel.\n\n**4. Kalenji Run Cushion — ₹1,399 — best cheap running-specific option**  \nA very attractive choice if you want to stay well below ₹2,000.\n\n**5. ASICS JOLT 4 — around ₹2,069 — best branded alternative**  \nCurrent 2026 price tracking puts it around ₹2,069, with an Ortholite sockliner and a more established running-shoe pedigree. [magicdrop.in](https://magicdrop.in/drops/best-running-shoes-under-3000?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### What I'd buy\n\n- **Running 3–5 km, 3–4×/week:** Jogflow 100.1\n- **Running 5–10 km regularly:** Jogflow 190.1\n- **Need more stability/support:** Kalenji Run Support\n- **Tightest budget:** Kalenji Run Cushion\n- **Want ASICS:** JOLT 4\n\nI wouldn't spend the full ₹3,000 just because you can—the **₹1,500–₹2,600 range currently has some excellent value**.\n\nIf you tell me **your gender, usual running distance (e.g. 3K/5K/10K), and whether you have wide feet**, I can narrow this to **one exact pair and size/fit advice**.",
